  "articleBody": "Deciding where to put a toilet grab bar can feel a bit tricky, but it's really about making sure it gives you the best support for how you move. Most folks find a horizontal grab bar on the side wall to be super helpful, especially when you're sitting down or standing up. It's often recommended to place it around 33-36 inches high from the floor. Think about it – that’s right where your hand naturally reaches. Sometimes, adding a bar on the back wall, perhaps diagonally, can offer extra stability, particularly if you need a bit more leverage. It really depends on your personal needs and what feels most secure for you. You want to make sure you have solid anchoring, so it's not just floating there, but really supporting your weight. If you're not sure about placement or your walls aren't straightforward, a professional can definitely help you figure out the optimal spot. They can make sure it's mounted correctly and safely, especially when dealing with tricky areas like tile.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}